      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T17:34:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, this particular approach will break discovery with TBT partners who don\u0027t tell us they run TBT until they get 15W.  So this might warrant waiting until the discovery refactor so it can be finer-grained...",
      "revId": "8b11173624c7e0c58d1b118a84e6de7024640ed0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "93c0e035_cd9a8f53",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2927,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T18:16:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The scenarios should be mutually exclusive, right? If the partner is self-powered, it won\u0027t need to wait for us to supply 15W to offer TBT (ignoring that this is the wrong way to do it). If the partner is not self-powered, it won\u0027t need to discover the cable to decide whether to offer 5A.",
      "parentUuid": "15d2f14c_ec3b5d51",
      "revId": "8b11173624c7e0c58d1b118a84e6de7024640ed0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4783a47b_e13a1241",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2927,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-12T18:47:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, so for the self-powered partner we\u0027d want to prioritize the Get_Sink_Caps and then the Source_Cap update before discovery.\n\nFor the partners that could source us, we\u0027d want to prioritize discovery and entry before we then ask for their source caps and decide to PR swap (both for vconn swap considerations and also to shorten time to EnterMode). \n\nAt the moment, all of the non-discovery parts are grouped together into source_dpm_requests(), which makes this somewhat tricky to tune without starting to break apart that function and the common DPM requests function.",
      "parentUuid": "93c0e035_cd9a8f53",
      "revId": "8b11173624c7e0c58d1b118a84e6de7024640ed0",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
  ],
